## ABSTRACT
Considering the tremendous applications and purification requirement of acetylene \(\left(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}\right)\), seeking appropriate adsorbents with high capacity and selectivity is a vital task and remains an enduring challenge. Herein, we designed and synthesized a robust three-dimensional (3D) indium-organic framework \(((\mathsf{M e})_{2}\mathsf{N H}_{2}][\mathsf{I n}(\mathsf{L}_{6})_{0.5}(\mathsf{I P A})_{0.5}]\cdot\mathsf{D M A}\cdot2\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}\) (In-L6-IPA, DMA = dimethylammonium, IPA = isopropyl alcohol)) featuring two types of one-dimensional (1D) tubular channels. The activated In-L6-IPA displayed high loading for \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}\) \((104.4\ \mathsf{c m}^{3}{\cdot}\mathsf{g}^{-1}\), the second highest value among all reported indium-based metal-organic frameworks (MOFs)) and simultaneously selective adsorption for \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}\) over \(\mathsf{C O}_{2}\), \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{6}\), and ethylene \(\left(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4}\right)\) at \(298~\mathsf{K}\) under 100 kPa. Molecular modelling revealed that the porous wall of In-L6-IPA provides more and stronger multiple interactions for \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}\) than \(\mathsf{C O}_{2}\), \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{6}\), and \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4}\) containing \(\mathsf{C{\mathrm{-}}H^{\ldots}\Pi}\), \(\mathsf{C{\mathrm{-}}H^{\ldots}O}\), and \(\mathsf{O^{\ldots}\Pi}\) interactions. Breakthrough experiments validated the actual separation ability for various ratios of binary \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}/\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4}\) and \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}/\mathsf{C O}_{2}\) mixtures as well as equimolar ternary \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}/\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4}/\mathsf{C O}_{2}\) and \(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}/\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{4}/\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{6}\) mixtures with excellent reusability.
## KEYWORDS
indium-organic framework, crystal structure, gas adsorption, acetylene \(\left(\mathsf{C}_{2}\mathsf{H}_{2}\right)\) separation
## 1 Introduction
Formed by connecting metal ions/clusters and organic linkers, metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) have been well demonstrated to be prominent candidates for numerous important applications such as water harvesting [17], sensing [18], heterogeneous catalysis [19, 20], energy storage [21], just to name a few. Especially owing to large surface areas, high modularity, powerful predictability, the emergence of MOFs enables the prospective design of target porous adsorbents with desirable properties for specific gas separations [22–28]. Although a large number of investigations have exhibited that MOFs display great separation performance for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) or \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) mixtures, their practical utilization is still limited owing to the poor stability. For instance, pillared square grid SIFSIX materials are considered to be promising candidates and display benchmark selectivity for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) or \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) separation [29, 30]. However, some SIFSIX materials were observed to decompose or undergo phase transformations under low levels of water and humidity conditions [31]. In addition, the well-established cases of MOF-74 series with open metal sites (OMSs) can bind \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) significantly, leading to the high \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake and moderate \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) selectivity [32, 33]. Nevertheless, it is well known that water molecules often act as competitors for OMSs.
Therefore, how to build moisture stable MOFs is of great significance for its industrial separation application. In general, the introduction of high-oxidation-state \(\mathrm{Ti}^{4+}\), \(\mathrm{Zr}^{4+}\), \(\mathrm{Al}^{3+}\), \(\mathrm{Cr}^{4+}\), and \(\mathrm{In}^{3+}\) ions to coordinate with carboxylic acid groups can easily generate
highly stable MOFs [34–37]. Among these MOFs, indium-based MOFs display more versatile coordination modes \(\left(\left[\mathrm{In}(\mathrm{O}_{2}\mathrm{CR})_{4}\right]\right.\), \(\left[\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{OH}-\mathrm{In}\right]_{n}\) and \(\left[\mathrm{In}_{3}\mathrm{O}(\mathrm{COO}_{2})_{6}(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})_{3}\right]\)) during the assembly with multicarboxylate ligands [38]. Up to now, the research of InMOFs is mainly focused on structure exploration, but the \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) separation performance has not been well investigated.
Inspired by these endeavors, we firstly designed and synthesized a new multicarboxylate ligand [1,1:3',1"-terphenyl]-3,3',4',5,5',6'-hexacarboxylic acid with \(\mathrm{In}^{3+}\) ions to fabricate MOFs, taking into account the following: (1) Stable coordination bonds between hard base O atoms and hard acid \(\mathrm{In}^{+}\)ions prefer to form robust MOFs; (2) the abundance of aromatic phenyl units of ligands can result a nonpolar pore environment, which significantly improves the humid stability of the framework. Herein, a robust indium-based MOF \(\left(\left[(\mathrm{Me})_{2}\mathrm{NH}_{2}\right]\left[\mathrm{In}(\mathrm{C}_{6})_{0.5}(\mathrm{IPA})_{0.5}\right]\cdot\mathrm{DMA}\cdot2\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\right.\) \(\left(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA},\right.\) DMA \(=\) dimethylammonium, \(\mathrm{IPA}=\) isopropyl alcohol) with open tubular channels has been constructed and shows excellent resistance in humidity and air environment. The activated \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\) IPA displays high loading for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) of \(104.4\;\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(298\;\mathrm{K}\) under \(100\ \mathrm{kPa}\), which is the second highest value among all reported indium-based MOFs. The \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) selective adsorption behaviors over \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6}\), and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) have been evidenced by ideal adsorbed solution theory (IAST) and separation potential calculations. Grand canonical monte carlo (GCMC) calculation revealed that the porous wall of the \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) provides more and stronger multiple interactions for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) than \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\), \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6}\), and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\). The separation performance for various ratios of binary \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) mixtures as well as ternary \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}/\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}/\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6}\) mixtures have demonstrated by dynamic breakthrough experiments.
## 2 Results and discussion
## 2.1 Crystal structure and characterization
\(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) crystallizes in the tetragonal space group \(\bar{I}\bar{4}_{2}m\), and contains one independent \(\mathrm{In}^{3+}\) ion, a half \(\mathrm{L}_{6}^{6-}\) ligand, a half \(\mathrm{IPA}^{2-}\),
The powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) patterns of the as-synthesized \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) match with the simulated results from crystal structure, suggesting the phase purity of bulk samples (Fig. S4 in the ESM). Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) results reveal that the \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) displays an obvious weight loss before \(140\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\), corresponding to releasing all free \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) and DMA solvent molecules (calcd \(20.2\%\), found \(20\%\)) (Fig. S5 in the ESM). Nitrogen \(\left(\mathrm{N}_{2}\right)\) adsorption isotherm of dehydrated \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) at 77 K exhibits a typical fully reversible type-I isotherm with the saturated uptake of \(207.3\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\), indicating its permanent porosity and microporous characteristics (Fig. 2(a)). The Brunauer–Emmett–Teller (BET) and Langmuir surface area of \(\mathrm{In}-\mathrm{I}_{6}-\mathrm{IPA}\) are 688 and \(794\ \mathrm{m}^{2}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\), respectively. And the measured accessible pore volume of \(0.32\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) is lower than the theoretical value of \(0.7\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) calculated from crystal data, due to the existence of \(\mathrm{Me}_{2}\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{+}\)counterion in the pores. As depicted in Fig.
S6 in the ESM, the main pore size distribution of \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA is calculated to be \(6.4–9.3\mathrm{~\AA~}\) based on the density functional theory (DFT) model, consistent well with the result of crystallographic structure analysis.
## 2.2 Gas adsorption
The permanent microporosity and suitable pore size of \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA encouraged us to further investigate its \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) -related separation application. Therefore, single-component adsorption isotherms for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CO}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CH}_{4},\) \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6},\) and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) were recorded at 298 and \(273\,\mathrm{~K~}\) . As illustrated in Figs. 2(b) and 2(c), the \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake is obviously higher than those of other \(C_{2}/C_{1}\) hydrocarbons and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) . Under \(100\;\mathrm{kPa}\) , the saturated adsorption amounts of \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CO}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CH}_{4},\) \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6},\) and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) are 130.9, 101.9, 24.8, 71.9, and \(82.3\;\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(273\;\mathrm{K}\) and 104.4, 66.1, 15.7, 64.8, and \(67.3\;\mathrm{cm}^{3}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\) at \(298\,\mathrm{~K},\) respectively. Notably, the value of \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake at \(298\,\mathrm{~K~}\) was only lower than UPC-104 [39], ranked the second highest among all reported indium-based MOFs, as depicted in Fig. 2(d) and Table S3 in the ESM. The slight hysteresis for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) desorption curves may be attributed to strong interactions between the framework and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) molecules relative to other tested gases. Furthermore, the continuous \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) adsorption/ desorption curves at \(298\,\mathrm{~K},\) without further activation treatment showed no obvious loss in \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake at least five cycles (Fig. S7 in the ESM), indicating excellent recyclability and regeneration capability. The isosteric heat of adsorption \(\left(Q_{\mathrm{st}}\right)\) for \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA was determined by virial equation to assess the host–guest interactions between the gas molecules and framework (Figs. S8–S12 in the ESM). As demonstrated in Fig. 2(e), the zero-coverage \(Q_{\mathrm{st}}\) values for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CO}_{2},\) \(\mathrm{CH}_{4},\) \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{6},\) and \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{4}\) were computed to be 32.2, 28.3, 21.3, 30.1, and \(30.3\;\mathrm{kJ}{\cdot}\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\) , respectively, corroborating that \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA had a stronger thermodynamic affinity toward \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) than other gases. Figure 2(f) presents a comparison of \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA with some typical MOFs when we set \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake and zero-coverage \(Q_{\mathrm{st}}\) values of \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) as concurrent objectives. Notably, the \(Q_{\mathrm{st}}\) values of these gases were below \(35\ \mathrm{kJ{\cdot}m o l^{-1}}\) and lower than most reported MOFs, including NKMOF-1-Ni \((60.0\,\mathrm{~kJ{\cdot}m o l^{-1}})\) [40], \(\mathrm{Cu}^{\mathrm{i}}\mathrm{UiO-66-(COOH)}_{2}\) \((66.8\,\mathrm{~kJ{\cdot}m o l^{-1}})\) [41], TIFSIX-2-Cu-i \((52.5\ \mathrm{~kJ{\cdot}m o l^{-1}})\) [30], and ZJU-74a \((38.9\ \mathrm{~kJ{\cdot}m o l^{-1}})\) [5]. Taken together, \(\mathrm{In-L_{6}}\) -IPA displays a high \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) uptake as well as moderate \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) \(Q_{\mathrm{st}}\) value, which indicates a less energy consume, rendering it promising materials for \(\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{H}_{2}\) separation.
