## 4.2 Synthesis of In- \( \mathrm{L}_{6} \)-IPA
A mixture of [1,1;3;1"-terphenyl]-3,3",4',5,5",6'-hexacarboxylic acid \( \left(\mathrm{L}_{6}\right) \) (0.012 g), isophthalic acid \( \left(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{IPA}\right) \) (0.005 g), and \( \mathrm{In}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{3}{\cdot}x\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O} \) (0.025 g) was sealed in the mixed solvent of 3 mL DMA, 1 mL \( \mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O} \), and 4.5 mL \( \mathrm{HNO}_{3} \) (2.2 mL of \( \mathrm{HNO}_{3} \), in 10 mL of DMF) in 15 mL glass vial, and heated at 105 °C for 72 h to
obtain colorless needles of crystals (yield: \(31\%\), based on \(\mathrm{In}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{3}{\cdot}x\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\)). Anal. Calcd for \(\mathrm{C}_{22}\mathrm{H}_{27}\mathrm{N}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{11}\mathrm{In}\): C, \(43.29\%\); H, \(4.46\%\); N, \(4.59\%\). Found: C, \(43.11\%\); H, \(4.65\%\); N, \(4.34\%\).
